  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Telmisartan may be associated with Hypertensive Disorder through off-label use in the context of Diabetic Nephropathy. This association is supported by multiple pathways where Telmisartan is linked to Diabetic Nephropathy, which in turn is associated with other antihypertensive medications. Specifically, Telmisartan is used off-label to treat Diabetic Nephropathy, and this condition is linked to the use of Captopril, Losartan, and Irbesartan, all of which are indicated for Hypertensive Disorder. The consistent scores across the three paths (final_score=0.6519) indicate a plausible, though not definitive, relationship between Telmisartan and Hypertensive Disorder through this off-label use pathway. The evidence is supported by the shared indication chain and the overlapping clinical contexts, but the exact mechanism of how Telmisartan contributes to Hypertensive Disorder remains uncertain. The strength of the evidence is moderate, and further research would be needed to confirm the causal relationship.",
